@* Album art for a tile, and a square that looks deliberate when there isn't any.

   Whether an album has a cover is only knowable by going and looking — AlbumArtService checks
   for an adjacent cover.jpg and then parses an ID3 tag, on a file that may be on a NAS. Asking
   that fifty times to render one page of a grid would put a network round trip in front of the
   markup, so nothing here asks: the browser requests the art lazily and the endpoint answers 404
   when there is none, which the placeholder underneath is already sized and styled for.

   The img is removed on error rather than hidden, because a broken <img> is drawn differently by
   every browser and one of the drawings is a grey icon in the middle of the tile. *@

<span class="cover" aria-hidden="true">
    @if (AlbumId is { } id)
    {
        <img class="cover__art" src="@($"/art/album/{id}")" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             onerror="this.remove()" />
    }
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>Null when there is no album to ask about — an artist with nothing playable.</summary>
    [Parameter] public Guid? AlbumId { get; set; }
}
